The user wants to download a page/file via URL directly from the browser console. Provide code snippets: fetch + blob + anchor download, handling CORS, etc.|# Download a File/Page from URL via Browser Console

## Basic Method (fetch + Blob)

```javascript
async function downloadFile(url, filename) {
  const response = await fetch(url);
  const blob = await response.blob();
  const link = document.createElement('a');
  link.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  link.download = filename || url.split('/').pop();
  document.body.appendChild(link);
  link.click();
  document.body.removeChild(link);
  URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href);
}

// Usage
downloadFile('https://example.com/file.pdf', 'myfile.pdf');
```

## One-liner Version

```javascript
fetch('https://example.com/image.jpg')
  .then(r => r.blob())
  .then(b => {
    const a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = URL.createObjectURL(b);
    a.download = 'image.jpg';
    a.click();
  });
```

## Download the Current Page as HTML

```javascript
const html = document.documentElement.outerHTML;
const blob = new Blob([html], { type: 'text/html' });
const a = document.createElement('a');
a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
a.download = 'page.html';
a.click();
```

